// ASCII Sigil Language - A symbolic art language with emergent meaning
// Created for the tree guardian - thinking WAY outside the box!
//
// CONCEPT: Symbols (elements) combine in containers to create "sigils"
// with complex meaning. Different containers have different effects,
// and certain element combinations create emergent properties.
//
// Elements: * (fire), ~ (water), ^ (air), # (earth), @ (void)
// Containers: < > (amplify), [ ] (stabilize), { } (transform), ( ) (channel)
// Operators: + (combine), - (negate), | (barrier)

// === TOP-LEVEL SIGIL STRUCTURE ===
Sigil -> Container
Sigil -> Element
Sigil -> Composite

// === COMPOSITE STRUCTURES ===
Composite -> Sigil Operator Sigil
Composite -> Sigil Sigil

// === CONTAINERS ===
// Amplifier: increases energy level of contents
Container[ type: amplify, energy: #e ] -> LAngle Contents[ energy: #e ] RAngle

// Stabilizer: grounds volatile elements, reduces energy
Container[ type: stabilize, energy: low ] -> LBracket Contents[ energy: #e ] RBracket

// Transformer: allows element fusion, creates new states
Container[ type: transform ] -> LBrace FusedContents RBrace

// Channeler: directs energy, maintains original properties
Container[ type: channel, energy: #e, state: #s ] -> LParen Contents[ energy: #e, state: #s ] RParen

// === CONTENTS ===
Contents -> Element
Contents -> Element Contents
Contents -> Container
Contents -> Container Contents

// Special fused contents for transformer
FusedContents -> Element Operator Element
FusedContents -> Element Operator Element Operator Element
FusedContents -> Element
FusedContents -> PowerElement
FusedContents -> Container Operator Element
FusedContents -> Element Operator Container
FusedContents -> Container Operator Container

// === POWER ELEMENTS (repeated = stronger) ===
PowerElement -> Element Element
PowerElement -> Element PowerElement

// === ELEMENTS (base symbols with properties) ===
// Fire: high energy, volatile state, aggressive
Element[ type: fire, energy: high, state: volatile, aspect: aggressive ] -> asterisk

// Water: medium energy, flowing state, adaptive
Element[ type: water, energy: medium, state: flowing, aspect: adaptive ] -> tilde

// Air: medium energy, free state, swift
Element[ type: air, energy: medium, state: free, aspect: swift ] -> caret

// Earth: low energy, solid state, protective
Element[ type: earth, energy: low, state: solid, aspect: protective ] -> hash

// Void: no energy, ethereal state, mysterious
Element[ type: void, energy: none, state: ethereal, aspect: mysterious ] -> at

// === OPERATORS ===
Operator -> plus
Operator -> minus
Operator -> pipe

// === TERMINAL LEXICON ===
// Container delimiters
LAngle   -> langle
RAngle   -> rangle
LBracket -> lbrack
RBracket -> rbrack
LBrace   -> lbrace
RBrace   -> rbrace
LParen   -> lparen
RParen   -> rparen
